Author: Codex Review <codex-review@example.invalid>
Date:   Tue Jun 2 22:36:39 2026 +0000

    fix(codegen): persist auto-deref two-level field/array stores (pointer root)
    
    Sibling of the explicit-deref fix: `name.f1.f2 = x` and `name.f1.f2[i] = x` where
    `name` binds a pointer/ref (*mut, &!) — the auto-deref form, written WITHOUT an
    explicit `(* )`. These ident-rooted two-hop stores had no dedicated detector and
    fell through to the generic assignment path, which (for a pointer root) wrote into
    a discarded value-copy of the inner struct — silently lost, read back as 0.
    
    This is the form used by the in-place checker's c.algebras.count / c.studies.count /
    c.ontologies.count collectors (the explicit (*c).fn_sigs.* collector is covered by
    the prior commit), so both halves of the #1 front-half lever's write shapes are now
    handled.
    
    Fix: stmt_is_field_field_store_shape / _array_store_shape (token-shape only) gated
    in dispatch on token_chain_root_is_pointer(EP). VALUE-struct roots return false and
    fall through to the generic path UNCHANGED (verified no regression). Pointer roots
    route to compile_autoderef_field_field_store_x86 / _array_store_x86, mirroring the
    explicit-deref codegen with ident-root token offsets.
    
    Evidence (worktree off g1/e008-bridge-fix, bootstrap = main bin/souc 9d4ef541):
    - repro/nested_autoderef_field_store_min.sio: was `top=9 n=0 v0=0`, now `top=9 n=3 v0=7`.
    - tests/run-pass/nested_mut_ref_struct_field.sio (the pre-existing G1b regression
      test: nested `&!Outer` field store o.inner.x=v propagating to caller) flips
      rc=1 (panic "FAIL") -> rc=0 ("OK"). This is a real, test-asserted correctness win.
    - explicit-deref repro + aggregate-elem checker pattern still green.
    - bootstrap fixed point holds: gen2==gen3 (md5 bd35d8ed…).
    - tests/run-pass sweep (504) ds_clean(no fix) vs both-fixes: identical compile set
      (476/476), 0 compile divergences, 1 improvement (G1b above), 0 real run
      divergences (3 apparent diffs are ASLR stack-address prints).
    
    Scope unchanged from prior commit: x86 only (a64 dispatch twin UNMODIFIED, still
    falls through — no cross-arch coverage); 3+-hop stores still fall through. The
    value-struct (non-pointer) `o.f1.f2` nested store is a SEPARATE pre-existing gap on
    this base (tracked by the main checkout's stmt_is_nested_field_store WIP), correctly
    left to the generic path here.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

